{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1053432-what-do-immaculate-monks-call-lunars","id":1053432,"title":"What do immaculate monks call Lunars.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-22T14:51:37-08:00","id":1053432,"title":"What do immaculate monks call Lunars.","content":"I have been reading around here that most DB and the public at large do not realize that the Lunar's are another type of Exalted. I realize that they will likely be lumped under anathama with everything that goes bump in the night. But","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12422-zylosan","name":"zylosan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T14:53:56-08:00","id":1053436,"title":"","content":"The only Immaculate epithet for Lunars that I'm ever able to remember are Ogres (which are for the No Moons, I think) and Moon-Mad for the Casteless.<br /> <br /> \u200bHmm, rephrase: I'm only able to ever remember half of the Immaculate epithets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T15:02:19-08:00","id":1053445,"title":"","content":"I can't remember where I read this, but I agree with it.<br /> <br /> The Lunars would actually be the Immaculate Order's most common template for Anathema, as they have been the only celestial exalts being hunted during the majority of the Imperial time. The return of the Solars would be like the return of the legendary demon princes to their lore, while the Lunars are the thing one thinks of with the general term 'Anathema'<br /> <br /> I can imagine that Immaculates would be more likely to refer to Lunar exalts more broadly as Anathema while using the caste-specific epithets for the Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Visit me at <a href=\"http://www.bragrman.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Tales of Grey</i></a> - my RPG Game-Master's blog.<br /> <br /> &quot;If only I had an enemy bigger than my apathy, I could have won&quot; - <i>I gave you all,</i> Mumford &amp; Sons","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8520-capitantypo","name":"CapitanTypo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8520_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"896"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T15:05:54-08:00","id":1053446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1053432-what-do-immaculate-monks-call-lunars?p=1053436#post1053436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only Immaculate epithet for Lunars that I'm ever able to remember are Ogres (which are for the No Moons, I think) and Moon-Mad for the Casteless.<br /> <br /> \u200bHmm, rephrase: I'm only able to ever remember half of the Immaculate epithets.</div> </div> </div> </div>The other ones you're looking for are frenzied and tricksters, you can guess which is which.<br /> <br /> As to general lunar terms, moon thieves and moon demons might be some they would use. Immaculate propaganda has it that lunar and solar anathema resemble the divine sun and moon because they stole their power long ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T15:14:27-08:00","id":1053456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1053432-what-do-immaculate-monks-call-lunars?p=1053446#post1053446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to general lunar terms, moon thieves and moon demons might be some they would use. Immaculate propaganda has it that lunar and solar anathema resemble the divine sun and moon because they stole their power long ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. Where is this from?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9061-tyranny12","name":"tyranny12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9061_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T16:19:47-08:00","id":1053492,"title":"","content":"Per the Immaculate demonology boxes in MoEP: Lunars, Casteless are Moon Mad, Full Moons are the Frenzied, Changing Moons are Tricksters, and No Moons are Ogres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T16:25:01-08:00","id":1053494,"title":"","content":"Don't forget barbarians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T16:28:58-08:00","id":1053497,"title":"","content":"I am curious about what the initial question of this thread was going to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T17:09:28-08:00","id":1053519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CapitanTypo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1053432-what-do-immaculate-monks-call-lunars?p=1053445#post1053445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't remember where I read this, but I agree with it.<br /> <br /> The Lunars would actually be the Immaculate Order's most common template for Anathema, as they have been the only celestial exalts being hunted during the majority of the Imperial time. The return of the Solars would be like the return of the legendary demon princes to their lore, while the Lunars are the thing one thinks of with the general term 'Anathema'<br /> <br /> I can imagine that Immaculates would be more likely to refer to Lunar exalts more broadly as Anathema while using the caste-specific epithets for the Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>My brother has made interesting use of this by having characters assume Solars will be able to shapechange, since they're Anathema and everyone knows Anathema can do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12816-diagrapher","name":"diagrapher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12816_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T17:18:19-08:00","id":1053523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zylosan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1053432-what-do-immaculate-monks-call-lunars#post1053432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have been reading around here that most DB and the public at large do not realize that the Lunar's are another type of Exalted. I realize that they will likely be lumped under anathama with everything that goes bump in the night. But</div> </div> </div> </div>Anathema is a fairly broad word that encompasses nearly everything under the sun (and moon). Fair Folk, ghosts, particularly evil spirits and even powerful or dangerous mortals could in theory be labeled Anathema. Essentially &quot;Anathema&quot; is a term that refers to any sort of being who poses a threat mortals (or at least to the Dragon Blooded's hegemony over the world.). However, among all of the Anathema, of particular note are the Solar Anathema and the Luna Anathema.<br /> <br /> According to Immaculate myth, the Solars and Lunars were great heroes who rose to rule the world. At some point they were swayed by demons (or perhaps they were always demons) and performed dark rituals to steal the power of the Sun and Moon. From there they ruled for a countless Age of Nightmares until the Immaculate Dragons appeared and helped to lead the Dragon Blooded to overthrow their oppressors.<br /> <br /> While a Fair Folk or a Spirit might be labeled an Anathema, it might not be labeled as one depending on its individual actions. Such beings who obey the dictates laid out by the Dragon Blooded aren't going to be viewed as Anathema and hunted down and killed for the most part. However, Lunars and Solars are <i>always</i> Anathema because their inherent existence is viewed as an existential threat to Creation itself and the Immaculate Order makes certain that everyone is aware of the most obvious signs of the Anathema (their caste marks, anima banners, Lunar shapeshifting, etc) so that they can be hunted down.<br /> <br /> So Lunars get singled out as Lunar Anathema and their castes are given their own unique sobriquets as Isator mentions (Full Moons are called The Frenzied, Half-Moons are The Tricksters, No-Moons are The Ogres and casteless are The Moon-Mad). Solars are known as Solar Anathema and are viewed in much the same way (though ultimately they're considered even more dangerous).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 02-22-2017, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T17:56:11-08:00","id":1053545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tyranny12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1053432-what-do-immaculate-monks-call-lunars?p=1053456#post1053456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting. Where is this from?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that is from the Immaculate Order section of the Blessed Isle book, but I can't be sure. It is somewhere official though. I found it when I went looking for why the Immaculate Order still worships the Sun and Moon but hates and hunts their chosen, and I found the story about them actually stealing power from the righteous and good gods and using it for evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T06:39:53-08:00","id":1053786,"title":"","content":"That's been the case since the very 1st ed Core. The Anathema were either demons or high priests of the Yozis or maybe heroic people who became demons (it's not very clear), but what is clear is that they stole their power from the Sun and Moon.<br /> <br /> I guess it's a good explanation for why Solars have a very obvious connection with the UCS and Lunars with Luna. If Solars claim they have UCS-themed powers because he gave it to them, Immaculates can say they stole it; it still explains the theme of the power. For example, if a Solar turns up and burns Hungry Ghosts with his sun-powers, it might be easy for him to say &quot;clearly a demon couldn't wield the power of the King of the Gods!&quot;, were it not for the fact that the Immaculates already know that.<br /> <br /> The best lies have a grain of truth, after all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My brother has made interesting use of this by having characters assume Solars will be able to shapechange, since they're Anathema and everyone knows Anathema can do that. <hr /> </div> </div> </div>I've done that. Also had people assume that they want to have sex with animals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T07:40:05-08:00","id":1053813,"title":"","content":"Swan: Stop! Take one more step, and I'll breathe fire on you!<br /> Arianna: He'll do it. He's crazy!<br /> Sad Ivory: Can they really breathe fire or did we make that up?<br /> \u200bChejop Kejak: Gee, I can't remember anymore. It might just be from those stupid Immaculate Texts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T08:36:05-08:00","id":1053835,"title":"","content":"I tend to run Immaculates as staying close to their &quot;official&quot; terms for Lunars and Solars: Blasphemous, Moon Mad, the Solar Anathema, and so on.<br /> <br /> I tend to run normal folk as either mangling the terms or inventing pejoratives: &quot;bloody moon demons,&quot; etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T09:54:14-08:00","id":1053861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1053432-what-do-immaculate-monks-call-lunars?p=1053813#post1053813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Swan: Stop! Take one more step, and I'll breathe fire on you!<br /> Arianna: He'll do it. He's crazy!<br /> Sad Ivory: Can they really breathe fire or did we make that up?<br /> \u200bChejop Kejak: Gee, I can't remember anymore. It might just be from those stupid Immaculate Texts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that you mention it, exhaling flames was something mentioned in the first edition core as being Solar-ish...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T10:17:28-08:00","id":1053866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1053432-what-do-immaculate-monks-call-lunars?p=1053813#post1053813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Swan: Stop! Take one more step, and I'll breathe fire on you!<br /> Arianna: He'll do it. He's crazy!<br /> Sad Ivory: Can they really breathe fire or did we make that up?<br /> \u200bChejop Kejak: Gee, I can't remember anymore. It might just be from those stupid Immaculate Texts.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the danger with propaganda, robot or otherwise.<br /> <br /> I used to have a PC (and a few NPCs) that would regularly threaten to eat people's souls. Because that seems like something Anathema can do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T10:29:57-08:00","id":1053878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1053432-what-do-immaculate-monks-call-lunars?p=1053813#post1053813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Swan: Stop! Take one more step, and I'll breathe fire on you!<br /> Arianna: He'll do it. He's crazy!<br /> Sad Ivory: Can they really breathe fire or did we make that up?<br /> \u200bChejop Kejak: Gee, I can't remember anymore. It might just be from those stupid Immaculate Texts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorcerous initiation by an ifrit. Sorcerous working. Red jade Artifacts. Etc. Swan COULD be fire-capable. I think it would be a bad idea, generally, to call a bluff in <i>Exalted</i> on the basis that one type of Exalted doesn't have access to some ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T10:57:59-08:00","id":1053890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>diagrapher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1053432-what-do-immaculate-monks-call-lunars?p=1053519#post1053519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My brother has made interesting use of this by having characters assume Solars will be able to shapechange, since they're Anathema and everyone knows Anathema can do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is solid. Lunars are the default Anathema to characters because they're the ones who've been running around for the last thousand years in a showy manner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T11:39:30-08:00","id":1053920,"title":"","content":"Exactly. It's something the 2nd ed books often seemed to forget, somehow making Solars the default.<br /> I hope that 3rd ed will change that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T04:14:01-08:00","id":1054260,"title":"","content":"Are we ever going to see where the end of the sentence in that first